&lt;p&gt;Robinhood&#39;s Enterprise Security team is at the forefront of AI security, designing safety guardrails for cutting-edge AI and driving modern enterprise-wide security tooling standards. As a Senior Corporate Security Engineer on our Corporate Systems team, you will operate at the center of our enterprise security infrastructure, maintaining the control plane for user-facing security tooling and building innovative solutions that keep our employees and platform secure!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will combine security engineering, systems administration, and hands-on AI agent development to drive key automation and safety initiatives. Joining a lean, high-impact team, you will have high visibility and direct empowerment to take strategic initiative, solve complex technical challenges, and shape Robinhood&#39;s AI security posture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is based in our Menlo Park or Bellevue office(s), with in-person attendance expected at least 3 days per week.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Robinhood, we believe in the power of in-person work to accelerate progress, spark innovation, and strengthen community. Our office experience is intentional, energizing, and designed to fully support high-performing teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, maintain, and evolve enterprise security tools that power key user-facing security flows, including endpoint security, login/authentication, and security telemetry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Secure AI interactions across the company by designing safety guardrails and integrating agentic tools into enterprise workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automate evidence-gathering processes for Governance, Risk, and Compliance (GRC) and internal/external regulatory audits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support enterprise vulnerability management programs and maintain operational resilience and uptime across core systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tackle evolving enterprise security challenges, such as protecting against active persistent threats (APTs) and securing the digital footprint of our executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally with Security Operations, GRC, Legal, and IT engineering partners to maintain a seamless, high-trust security environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of professional experience in information security, combining security engineering, IT systems administration, and enterprise infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in one or more of the following: managing and securing modern identity systems (e.g., Okta), or deep experience blending security engineering with systems/infrastructure engineering. (We&#39;re hiring for two closely related roles on this team — identity platform depth is a strong plus for one, broader security+ systems generalist range for the other.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to or hands-on experience with AI tools and agent workflows (e.g., OpenAI, Claude, Cursor, or custom API integrations).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience working within cloud environments (specifically Google Cloud Platform) and modern software development processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Broad security generalist skill set, including device compliance enforcement, binary/plugin/extension evaluation, behavior tracing, vulnerability management, and security policy enforcement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ownership mentality with an adaptable &quot;builder&quot; mindset, capable of driving automation and technical initiatives independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
