&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct and design Robinhood’s global tax planning and tax strategy, ensuring alignment with our expanding operations and business complexity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee and manage the international corporate tax lifecycle, including transfer pricing, inter-company agreements, legal entity maintenance, and global tax compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee all aspects of indirect tax strategy and compliance, including VAT, GST, sales tax, digital services taxes, and related international consumption tax matters across multiple jurisdictions.Provide guidance on tax matters for mergers, acquisitions, and restructuring activities, ensuring optimal integration of tax considerations into deal structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee and provide guidance on all federal, state, and local income tax operation for various pass-through and fund structures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, mentor, and develop a high-performing tax team, including managing managers and senior tax professionals across compliance, provision, and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with product, accounting, legal, and treasury departments to evaluate the tax implications of new products, operational flows, legal entity structure, and international expansion initiatives to support tax-efficient business growth and ensure compliance with global tax requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct the global income tax provision (ASC 740) and tax compliance, ensuring accurate reporting and strong internal controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the tax department in discussions with executive leadership and external auditors on complex international tax and structuring matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 15+ years of corporate tax experience, with a heavy emphasis on international tax planning, strategy, and compliance within a multinational corporation or major public accounting firm.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience as a people leader, with a track record of hiring, mentoring, and scaling high-performing tax teams (including managing managers).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in international tax concepts, transfer pricing, inter-company agreements, legal entity structuring, and ASC 740 tax provisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills, with the ability to explain complex global tax structures and reporting requirements to executive leaders and board members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, or equivalent practical experience; a CPA, Master of Taxation, or JD/LLM is highly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership expectations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our ambitious roadmap requires a great culture shaped by exceptional leaders. Here’s what we expect from them:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive high performance by setting clear, focused goals, giving real-time feedback, stretching top talent, and scaling impact through focus, innovation, and tech.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire and retain top talent by setting a high bar, hiring only those who raise it, investing in onboarding, and addressing talent issues quickly and fairly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create community by connecting work to purpose, removing friction while prioritizing safety, building trust and inclusion, and leading from the front with integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
